  "tag_ids": [],
  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00001",
      "text": "In a world first, Australia and New Zealand have created a “travel bubble” allowing people to move between the two countries without COVID-19 quarantine. It will enable family members to visit their relatives, as well as boosting tourism. Approximately 500,000 New Zealanders live in Australia, whilst 60,000 Australians live in New Zealand.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 341,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_New_Zealanders",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Zealand_Australians"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00002",
      "text": "In March 2020 both nations closed their borders to non-citizens and non-residents. Some exceptions applied. New Zealanders have been able to enter some Australian states since October 2020 but this freedom of movement was not reciprocated due to locally transmitted Covid-19 cases in Australia. This latest development follows the virtual elimination of community-transmitted cases in the country. Victoria – the worst affected state last year, which endured a four-month lockdown – has seen no local transmission for more than seven weeks.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 343,
      "body_end": 883,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_Australia#Travel"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00003",
      "text": "The two countries are separated by the Tasman Sea, affectionately referred to as “the ditch”. The term “trans-Tasman” usually applies to relationships between the nations or their peoples – in this case it's a shared travel zone.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 885,
      "body_end": 1114,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans-Tasman",
        "https://globalvoices.org/2016/10/04/the-updated-australian-national-dictionary-is-here-to-teach-you-dinkum-aussie-english/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00004",
      "text": "There are now direct flights between major cities in both countries., with 400 flights per week to and from Auckland expected to be running by the end of April.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 1116,
      "body_end": 1276,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00005",
      "text": "Flights from Australia to New Zealand began on April 19, with cheers and tears seen at departure and arrival areas.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1278,
      "body_end": 1393,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00006",
      "text": "Journalist Sophie Trigger, an Australian living in New Zealand, posted about her journey on Twitter:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1395,
      "body_end": 1495,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/Sophietrigger/status/1383942266222374923"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00007",
      "text": "Wellington resident Jessica Avery's response to the scenes at airports was typical of many:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1497,
      "body_end": 1588,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00008",
      "text": "The #transtasmanbubble Twitter hashtag provides no shortage of tear-jerking moments, such as this one witnessed by Australian Associated Press New Zealand correspondent Ben McKay:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1590,
      "body_end": 1769,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/search?q=%23transtasmanbubble%20&src=typed_query"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00009",
      "text": "However, there was a note of caution from at least one Twitter user:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1771,
      "body_end": 1839,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00010",
      "text": "According to The Guardian, this was a concern widely shared in New Zealand:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1841,
      "body_end": 1916,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/19/jacinda-ardern-heralds-very-significant-day-as-trans-tasman-travel-bubble-begins"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00011",
      "text": "> Despite that upbeat mood, the bubble still represents a risk for New Zealand’s Covid-free haven – and a political risk for Ardern’s government. It has been greeted with trepidation by the wider New Zealand public, with polling finding only around half of New Zealanders, or 49%, were in favour of opening the trans-Tasman bubble.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 1918,
      "body_end": 2249,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00012",
      "text": "There has been a push online for some time to open up a wider travel bubble with Pacific Ocean nations that have contained the coronavirus:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 2251,
      "body_end": 2390,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00013",
      "text": "Not everyone on social media was sure about this idea:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2392,
      "body_end": 2446,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00014",
      "text": "With very poor timing, this week Fiji recorded its first case of Covid-19 outside quarantine since March 2020:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2448,
      "body_end": 2558,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00015",
      "text": "Meanwhile, a border worker has tested positive in New Zealand, adding to concerns about international travel:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2560,
      "body_end": 2669,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00016",
      "text": "Tony Blakely, professor of Epidemiology at the University of Melbourne, has examined risks to Australia associated with international travel and travel bubbles at The Conversation:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2671,
      "body_end": 2851,
      "source_links": [
        "https://theconversation.com/whats-the-risk-if-australia-opens-its-international-borders-an-epidemiologist-explains-159208"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00017",
      "text": "> Here I propose three things we must consider:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 2853,
      "body_end": 2900,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00018",
      "text": "> the prevalence of the virus in the country from where travellers are coming, including the strain of virus",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 2902,
      "body_end": 3010,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00019",
      "text": "> measures taken for the people travelling, including home quarantine and whether travellers are vaccinated",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 3012,
      "body_end": 3119,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00020",
      "text": "> the percentage of our population who are immune.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 20,
      "body_start": 3121,
      "body_end": 3171,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00021",
      "text": "> Importantly, all these factors matter. It’s not simply a case of needing to ensure all travellers are vaccinated.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 21,
      "body_start": 3173,
      "body_end": 3288,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00022",
      "text": "> …we need a national framework to assess the risk. Focusing on one measure alone isn’t wise — you have to look at the whole system.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 22,
      "body_start": 3290,
      "body_end": 3422,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00023",
      "text": "It is inevitable that there will be pressures on the travel bubble when community transmission of COVID-19 occurs in either country. Quarantine-free travel from New Zealand was suspended by Australia in January 2021 because of a case of a South African strain of Covid-19 across the Tasman.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 23,
      "body_start": 3424,
      "body_end": 3714,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-01-25/greg-hunt-australia-new-zealand-travel-bubble-coronavirus/13089832"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-733993-b00024",
      "text": "The two-way system has been tested during its first week. New Zealand has paused travel from Perth, the State capital of Western Australia, as a result of a three-day lockdown there. A Victorian man tested positive after he completed 14 days quarantine at a Perth hotel and flew to Melbourne. Restrictions were also applied by NZ authorities to anyone on his flight and to exposure sites at the Melbourne Airport.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 24,
      "body_start": 3716,
      "body_end": 4129,
      "source_links": [
        "https://covid19.govt.nz/updates-and-resources/latest-updates/response-to-perth-3-day-lockdown/",
        "https://www.9news.com.au/national/new-corinavirus-restrictions-for-perth-after-another-positive-case-linked-to-hotel-outbreak/466da016-064e-4c13-968e-2cb2d7e2376b",
        "https://www.coronavirus.vic.gov.au/exposure-sites",
        "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/world/441154/covid-19-low-risk-to-nz-from-perth-case-health-ministry"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
